  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   - Central Idea: Augment the optimization process with domain-specific heuristics and mathematical insights derived from signal processing theory.\n   - Advantage: Exploits structure of the overlap integral and periodic signal properties, guiding search towards physically meaningful solutions.\n   - Bottleneck Addressed: Local optima by using frequency-based features and signal decomposition insights.\n   - Innovation: Introduces (1) harmonic scaling of feature maps to enhance correlation terms, (2) structured feature spaces motivated by Parseval's theorem, and (3) adaptive resolution merging based on Fourier analysis.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   - Variables: h(x) \u2208 [0,1] on [0,2] with \u222bh(x)dx=1\n   - Objective: C5(h,dx)=dx\u00d7max_k|<h(x)\u2225(1-h(x+k))>| (energy correlation)\n   - Constraint: Parseval-normalized Fourier coefficients |F\u0303(f)\u00b2| up to bandwidth B=2/n\n   - Representation: Piecewise-analytic form with bounded trigonometric basis\n   - Key Formulas:\n     \u2022 Fourier-based reconstruction: h(x) = \u03a3_{k=0}^{M} (a_k + b_k x)\n     \u2022 Parseval constraint: \u03a3_{k} |F\u0303(k)|\u00b2 = 4\n     \u2022 Smoothed objective: C5_S(h) = max_k [h(h(k)+h(k+k))-1] (approximated via FFT)\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   - 3.1. Initialization:\n        a. Prepare parent: h_parent = initial_h_values (n=256 samples)\n        b. Compute base Fourier features F = np.fft.rfft(h_parent)\n        c. Define solution space as {h : h(x) = \u03a3 c_k \u03c8_k(x)}\n           where \u03c8_k(x) = {sin(\u03c9_k x + \u03c6_k), cos(\u03c9_k x + \u03c6_k)}\n\n   - 3.2. Feature Design:\n        a. Frequency configuration:\n           - Primary modes: \u03c9\u2081 = 2\u03c0/1.5, \u03c9\u2082 = \u03c0/0.7\n           - \u03c6 variation: [0, 2\u03c0] uniform, size=5 designed experiments\n        b. Solve constrained optimization:\n           ```python\n           import cvxpy as cp\n           N = len(h_parent)-1\n           x = cp.Variable(N, boolean=True)\n           c1 = cp.Variable()\n           c2 = cp.Variable()\n           obj = cp.Minimize(1/c5_value(h_parent))  # Inverse C5 optimization\n           constr = [cp.sum(x)==N/2, c1>=0, c2<=1]\n           prob = cp.Problem(obj,constr)\n           prob.solve()\n           ```\n        c. Recovery: h_recovery = repair_h(x.value, N)\n\n   - 3.3. Candidate Generation:\n        a. Null-space feature generation:\n           ```python\n           A = np.array([cos(\u03c9xi), sin(\u03c9xi)] for \u03c9x in \u03c9_grid)\n           b = random.randn(A.shape[1])\n           x_proj = np.linalg.solve(np.dot(A.T, A), np.dot(A.T, b))\n           ```\n        b. L2-projection to piecewise-linear domain\n\n   - 3.4. Merging Framework:\n        ```python\n        for n_target in [128, 64, 32]:\n            h_coarse = reconstruction(h_parent, n_target)\n            score = c5_value(h_coarse,2/n_target)\n            if score < best_c5:\n                best = h_coarse\n        ```\n        uses:\n        - Fourier projection: templates = F[:n_target//2]\n        - Interpolation: np.interp(h_parent, x_source, x_target)\n\n   - 3.5. Repair Enforcement:\n        - Fourier-domain clipping: |F\u0303| < T_clip \u2192 0\n        - Iterative rescaling: normalize to energy constraint\n          ```python\n          def normalize_ftn(F):\n              norms = np.abs(F)\n              target = 4. * n_points / (2*len(norms))\n              scale = target / (np.sum(norms**2)**0.5)\n              return scale * F\n          ```\n\n4. Search Choices and Use Variations\n   - 4.1. Algorithm Variations:\n        a. Version 1: Base optimization + harmonic basis\n        b. Version 2: Quadrature-based refinement\n           - Quadrature weights for FFT kernel\n        c. Version 3: Wavelet-like packet decomposition\n           - Coefficients at \u0394 scales = [1, 2, 4]\n\n   - 4.2. Parameter Configurations:\n        Primary waves: \u03c9 from [1/3, 2/3] sampled logarithmically\n        Phase coverage: [0, 2\u03c0] randomized to cover Brillouin zone\n        Repetition: 7 patterns (each variation) for each scale\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n   - Hierarchical allocation:\n        n=512: approx 700s (main target)\n        n=256: 200s\n        n=128: 80s\n        n= Efficiency: O(n\u00b2) for merging, optimizers scale O(M\u00b3) for dimension M\n\n   - Stop conditions:\n        - Individual run: minimal improvement plateau\n        - Overall: 1300s expiration\n        - Failure: Fallback to parent via Fourier-projection\n        - NaN handling: Reject invalid candidate\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n   - Output checks:\n        \u2022 Fourier normalization: sum(|F\u0303|\u00b2) \u2248 2\u00b7n_points\n        \u2022 Clipping: only harmonic features survive\n        \u2022 Scale-independence: score computed for multiple n\n        \u2022 Repair validation: sum(h* in [0,1]), integral\u2248n/2\n\n   - Derived computes:\n        \u2022 C5_alt = np.max(np.abs(np.fft.irfft(F_proj, n)), else value\n        \u2022 Fourier-based score as secondary guide",
